<section id="migration" aria-labelledby="migration-heading" class="content-defer border-b border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
            @* Card 1: Easy KeePass (.kdbx) Import & Backup *@
            <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
                <div>
                    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-blue-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-file-import" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>KeePass (.kdbx) Import &amp; Backup</span>
                    </div>
                    <h2 id="migration-heading" class="mt-4 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">
                        Import or Back Up Your KeePass Database in Browser
                    </h2>
                    <p class="mt-3 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                        Already using KeePass or KeePassXC? Open the <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800">⋮</code> menu next to <strong>Current Vault</strong> and choose <strong>Import — From KeePass (.kdbx)</strong>. PassKee supports KDBX 3 and KDBX 4 files up to 100 MB while preserving your nested directories, credentials, tags, and file attachments.
                    </p>

                    <ol class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700">
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                            <span class="flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">1</span>
                            <span><strong>Select your .kdbx file &amp; password:</strong> Decrypted locally via WebAssembly—your KDBX database password is only used to unlock the file during import.</span>
                        </li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                            <span class="flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">2</span>
                            <span><strong>Re-encrypt with your Vault Key:</strong> Every directory, entry, and attachment is sealed with your PassKee <code class="font-mono text-xs">AES-256-GCM</code> key.</span>
                        </li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                            <span class="flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">3</span>
                            <span><strong>Backup to KDBX 4 anytime:</strong> Use <strong>Backup — Export to KeePass (.kdbx)</strong> to download an encrypted KDBX 4 backup (archived items are exported into an <code class="font-mono text-xs">Archive</code> folder).</span>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </div>

                <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-slate-100">
                    <a href="/registration" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-bold text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">
                        <span>Create your vault and import .kdbx</span>
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </article>

            @* Card 2: Effortless Encrypted Sharing *@
            <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
                <div>
                    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-share-nodes" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>Share a Link to This Item</span>
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">
                        Share Credentials Safely Without Plaintext Chats
                    </h2>
                    <p class="mt-3 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                        Need to send a login, database credential, or secure note to a colleague or family member? Click <strong>Share</strong> on any item to generate an end-to-end encrypted link instead of pasting plaintext secrets into Slack, Telegram, or email.
                    </p>

                    <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 space-y-3">
                        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-400">URL Fragment (#) Zero-Knowledge Format</p>
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-900 p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-300 break-all">
                            https://passkee.org/share/0195f8a27c4b<span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold">#8f9d2a7e4c1b09f3a5d6e7f8...</span>
                        </div>
                        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-600">
                            <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-check text-emerald-600" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                <span>The 64-character hex key after <code class="font-mono font-bold text-slate-800">#</code> is never transmitted to PassKee servers.</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-check text-emerald-600" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                <span>Set expiry (<code class="font-mono text-slate-800">1 hour</code>, <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">1 day</code>, <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">7 days</code>, <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">30 days</code>) and optional <strong>Can be viewed only once</strong>.</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-info-circle text-amber-600" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                <span>Attached files are never included in shared links.</span>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-slate-100">
                    <a href="/security#encrypted-sharing" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-bold text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">
                        <span>Read how #fragment encryption works</span>
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
